#Commands to install and try out RedPanda local#
mkdir redpanda
cd redpanda
curl -sSL https://docs.redpanda.com/redpanda-quickstart.tar.gz | tar xzf -
cd docker-compose
docker compose up -d

Make sure docker-desktop is installed in Windows and is running while executing "docker compose up -d"
If the above command executes successfully, Red Panda console should be visible in http://localhost:8080
Initially login with username - superuser and password - secretpassword
Change it after logging in


Change the docker-compose.yml according to your cluster requirements and start container again
docker-compose up -d 

#Create topic#
docker exec redpanda-local rpk topic create f1_live_telemetry

#Sending telemetry from python#
pip install kafka-python
